('112.6.b.12.A',3,'What gas do plants give off when they make food?','["nitrogen", "smoke", "carbon dioxide", "oxygen"]'::jsonb,3,'Plants release oxygen.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.A',3,'Which plant part takes in most of the sunlight?','["leaves", "bark", "roots", "seeds"]'::jsonb,0,'Leaves capture sunlight.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.A',3,'A plant is kept in a dark closet for two weeks. What will probably happen?','["it will make more food", "it will not make enough food and will weaken", "it will grow faster", "it will turn into an animal"]'::jsonb,1,'Without light, a plant cannot make food well.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.A',3,'Which of these is a producer?','["a hawk", "a rabbit", "a tree", "a snake"]'::jsonb,2,'A tree makes its own food.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.A',4,'Which statement describes the cycling of matter in a plant?','["plants destroy matter", "plants make carbon dioxide from sugar only", "plants create matter from nothing", "plants use carbon dioxide and water to make sugar"]'::jsonb,3,'Matter is cycled and rearranged.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.B',2,'What do decomposers do?','["break down dead plants and animals", "make food from sunlight", "give off light", "eat only living animals"]'::jsonb,0,'Decomposers recycle matter.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.B',3,'Which is a decomposer?','["a grass plant", "a mushroom", "a rabbit", "an owl"]'::jsonb,1,'Fungi decompose dead things.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.B',3,'In a food web, what is the source of energy for producers?','["the consumers", "the decomposers", "the Sun", "the soil"]'::jsonb,2,'Producers use sunlight.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.B',3,'A hawk eats a snake that ate a mouse. The hawk is what?','["a source of energy", "a producer", "a decomposer", "a consumer"]'::jsonb,3,'A hawk eats other animals.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.B',3,'Why are decomposers important?','["they return nutrients to the soil", "they stop energy flow", "they eat producers only", "they make sunlight"]'::jsonb,0,'They recycle nutrients.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.B',3,'Which arrow correctly shows energy flow?','["rabbit → grass", "grass → rabbit", "rabbit → Sun", "owl → grass"]'::jsonb,1,'Arrows point to the organism that gets the energy.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.B',4,'If all decomposers disappeared, what would happen?','["the Sun would stop shining", "more plants would grow quickly", "dead material would pile up and nutrients wouldn''t be recycled", "producers would turn into consumers"]'::jsonb,2,'Decomposers recycle matter.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.C',2,'What can fossils tell scientists?','["the temperature now", "tomorrow''s weather", "the age of a student", "what living things and environments existed long ago"]'::jsonb,3,'Fossils are evidence of the past.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.C',3,'Marine fossils such as shells are found on a hilltop in Texas. What does this suggest?','["the area was once under the sea", "the hill was always dry", "the shells fell from the sky", "shells grow on hills"]'::jsonb,0,'The fossils show an ancient ocean.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.C',3,'Dinosaur tracks found in Texas show that what once lived there?','["whales only", "dinosaurs", "dragons", "humans"]'::jsonb,1,'Texas has dinosaur trackways.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.C',3,'A fossil fern is found in a dry region. What can be concluded?','["ferns need no water", "the area was always dry", "the area was once wetter", "ferns are animals"]'::jsonb,2,'Ferns need moist places.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.C',3,'In which kind of rock are fossils MOST often found?','["igneous rock", "lava", "metamorphic rock", "sedimentary rock"]'::jsonb,3,'Layers of sediment preserve remains.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.C',3,'A fossil of a warm-water coral is found in a cold place today. What does this suggest?','["the place was once warmer", "corals like ice", "the coral moved by itself", "the place was always cold"]'::jsonb,0,'Corals live in warm water.','original'),
('112.6.b.12.C',4,'Why can fossils of sea animals be found far from the ocean today?','["wind carried shells from the sea", "oceans covered the land long ago", "sea animals walked there", "the ocean is closer than before"]'::jsonb,1,'Land that was once underwater became dry.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.A',2,'A cactus has waxy skin. How does this help it survive?','["it makes the cactus magnetic", "it makes the cactus taller", "it keeps water from escaping", "it attracts rain"]'::jsonb,2,'The wax holds water in.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.A',3,'Mesquite trees in Texas have very deep roots. How does this help them?','["they climb rocks", "they float on water", "they make seeds faster", "they reach water far underground"]'::jsonb,3,'Deep roots reach water.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.A',3,'A water lily has wide, flat leaves that float. What is the function?','["to catch sunlight at the water''s surface", "to dig into the mud", "to hide from fish", "to hold water inside"]'::jsonb,0,'Leaves float to get light.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.A',3,'A cactus has spines instead of broad leaves. How does this help it?','["it gets more sunlight", "it loses less water and is protected from animals", "it needs more water", "it hides underground"]'::jsonb,1,'Spines reduce water loss and defend the plant.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.A',3,'A pine tree has thin needle-shaped leaves. How do they help in cold, dry places?','["they fall off quickly", "they absorb more snow", "they lose less water", "they make the tree grow faster"]'::jsonb,2,'Needles reduce water loss.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.A',3,'A plant in a rainforest has leaves with pointed tips. How does this help it?','["it blocks light", "water collects on the leaf", "it traps insects", "water drips off easily"]'::jsonb,3,'Drip tips shed rainwater.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.A',4,'A desert wildflower blooms right after a rain and then makes seeds quickly. How does this help it?','["it can finish its life before the dry time returns", "it grows deeper roots than trees", "it avoids soil completely", "it uses sunlight at night"]'::jsonb,0,'A quick life cycle fits short wet periods.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.B',2,'Which is an INHERITED trait?','["knowing how to ride a bike", "eye color", "a haircut", "a scar on the knee"]'::jsonb,1,'Eye color is passed from parents.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.B',2,'Which is an ACQUIRED trait?','["the number of legs a spider has", "flower color", "a scar from a fall", "fur color in a dog"]'::jsonb,2,'Scars are gained during life.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.B',3,'A dog learns to sit on command. What kind of trait is this?','["both always", "inherited", "neither", "acquired"]'::jsonb,3,'Learned behaviors are acquired.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.B',3,'A tiger has stripes because its parents did. What kind of trait is this?','["inherited", "acquired", "temporary", "learned"]'::jsonb,0,'Stripes are passed from parent to offspring.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.B',3,'A person learns to play the piano. What kind of trait is this?','["inherited", "acquired", "genetic", "passed by eye color"]'::jsonb,1,'Skills are learned.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.B',3,'Which is NOT inherited?','["hair texture", "blood type", "a broken arm", "eye color"]'::jsonb,2,'Injuries are acquired.','original'),
('112.6.b.13.B',4,'A seedling is bent by wind and grows crooked. Its seeds grow into straight plants. What does this show?','["wind changes seeds", "the bend was inherited", "seeds always bend", "the bend was acquired and not inherited"]'::jsonb,3,'Acquired traits are not passed on.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Science' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
